Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 17:43:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03497/11362] [outer-loop] Q-head step 6: milestone-relabeling
 IMPLEMENTED, but blocked by the L2-SEED catch-22

Added milestone-distance re-labeling (Blind Squirrel's deepening mechanism) to SpatialValueNet:
label states by distance-to-NEXT-level-up across a multi-level trace (level-agnostic), so at
L1-complete the value targets steps-to-L2 (not 0, the v5 failure). The mechanism RUNS correctly.

But a clean DEEPENING demonstration is blocked by a catch-22, found via a 20-game L2-reachability
probe: only tu93 + vc33 reach L2 by blind exploration; tu93's L2 is a NON-REPRODUCIBLE parity
artifact (non-idempotent reset gotcha), and vc33's L2 is TRIVIALLY blind-reachable (blind reaches it
anyway, so milestone-relabeling shows no advantage: 800 vs blind/l1only ~580-931 exp, and the value
is mis-calibrated on thin 7-step seed data). The hard-L2 games where milestone-relabeling WOULD
matter have NO reproducible seed (L2 gradient-bound across all probed games).

CONCLUSION: milestone-relabeling is the right value-DEEPENING mechanism (matches the 2nd-place team)
but the BINDING constraint is upstream -- reaching a reproducible HARD-L2 seed, which is gradient-
bound. The SOTA leader (Executable World Models) sidesteps this via PROGRAM generalization
(induce+verify+refactor a transition/goal model), NOT value-relabeling. That program-generalization
path is the genuine next deepening lever, per the leaderboard research.

verdict: complete: L2_trivially_blind_reachable_no_deepening_advantage_demonstrable_on_this_seed

